Package: qphotorec
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @SHLIBS_DEPENDS@
Recommends: testdisk
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://www.cgsecurity.org/wiki/PhotoRec
Description: graphical file recovery tool (Qt front end to PhotoRec)
 QPhotoRec is the Qt GUI for PhotoRec, the file carver from the TestDisk
 project. It recovers lost files (photos, video, documents, archives and
 several hundred other formats) from hard disks, memory cards, USB sticks
 and disk images by reading the raw data, ignoring the filesystem.
 .
 Ubuntu's testdisk package ships testdisk, photorec and fidentify but is
 built without Qt, so it has no qphotorec. This package is upstream
 testdisk-7.2 built for arm64 and contains only qphotorec, its man page,
 desktop file and icons. Run it as root (sudo -E qphotorec) to see disks.
